
== 1. Dirichlet comb-tooth linewidth (Hayes Eq. 1: delta_nu ~ nu_R/N) ===========
  N =    64:  amplitude FWHM = 1.206817 nu_R/N,   intensity FWHM = 0.885986 nu_R/N
  N =   256:  amplitude FWHM = 1.206716 nu_R/N,   intensity FWHM = 0.885899 nu_R/N
  N =  1024:  amplitude FWHM = 1.206710 nu_R/N,   intensity FWHM = 0.885893 nu_R/N
  analytic half-widths: amplitude 1.895494/pi, intensity 1.391558/pi -> 0.603354, 0.442947 nu_R/N
  the widely quoted 0.886 is the INTENSITY (power-spectrum) value

== 2. Tooth amplitudes g_k, intensity sum rule, tooth-pair sums (Lee Eq. 1; APB Eqs. 20-22) 
  nu_rep = 120 MHz, tau = 14 ps, nu_rep*tau = 1.680e-03
  sum rule   sum_k g_k^2 / g_0^2 = 1.000000000000   (asymptotic in nu_rep*tau, not algebraic)
     at nu_rep*tau =  0.1: sum = 1.0000095
     at nu_rep*tau =  1.0: sum = 3.1416803
     at nu_rep*tau =  5.0: sum = 15.7079633
  tooth-pair overlap  sum_k g_k g_{k+l} / g_0^2   vs   sech(pi l nu_rep tau)   vs the WRONG sech(2 pi l nu_rep tau):
     l =    0:  exact 1.000000   sech(pi l..) 1.000000   sech(2pi l..) 1.000000
     l =   10:  exact 0.998145   sech(pi l..) 0.998609   sech(2pi l..) 0.994455
     l =  105:  exact 0.821226   sech(pi l..) 0.863911   sech(2pi l..) 0.595332
  -> at l = 105 the wrong argument gives 0.595 for 0.864, a 27% error; the closed form is itself ~5% high against the exact convolution
  APB point (nu_rep = 80 MHz, tau = 10 ps, n = 158, omega_q tau = 0.794371):
     tooth-pair sum          = 0.902128
     (omega_q tau)/sinh(..)  = 0.902088   [1 - x^2/6]
     sech(omega_q tau/2)     = 0.925994   [1 - x^2/8]  <- APB Eq. 22, the form to implement
     Hayes field-sech form (omega_q tau/2)/sinh(omega_q tau/2) at tau = 1 ps: 0.999737   [1 - x^2/24]
     gap between the first two: 2.65%  -- record, do not harmonize

== 3. Rosen-Zener single-pulse ceiling and the ONE sech(omega_q tau/2) factor ===
  sech^2(pi nu_HF T) at T = 14.8 ps: 0.720860
  sech^2(pi nu_HF T) at T = 14.0 ps: 0.744926
  sech^2(pi nu_HF T) at T =  7.6 ps: 0.914142
  unit discriminator: nu_HF read as ANGULAR at 14.8 ps -> 0.002474  (against the measured 72%)
  two-pulse full-transfer threshold 2 arccosh(sqrt2)/omega_q = 22.190 ps; qubit period 1/nu_HF = 79.096 ps
  ONE factor, three faces, all equal at tau = 10 ps: sech(omega_q tau/2) = 0.925994
     applied twice -> 0.857465, three times -> 0.794007  (spurious)
  sech intensity FWHM = 2 arccosh(2)/pi = 0.8384014366 tau; a sech^2 intensity envelope gives 0.5611 tau

== 4. Pulse-train-to-CW map: N = f_rep t, Omega_0 = f_rep theta (APB Eq. 23 defect) 
  worked example: Omega/2pi = 1 MHz at f_rep = 80 MHz, tau = 10 ps
     Omega_0/2pi = 1.07992 MHz, theta = Omega_0/f_rep = 0.08482 rad
     per-pulse Bloch angle varphi = theta sech(..) = 0.07854 rad  -> pi pulse in 40.0 pulses
  printed Omega_0 = 2 pi omega_rep theta would give theta = 2.148e-03 rad, too small by (2 pi)^2 = 39.478

== 5. Intensity-to-Rabi chain, signed fine-structure detunings, Chain I / Chain II E_pi 
  1/Delta = 1/Delta_1/2 - 1/Delta_3/2 with +33 and -67 THz  ->  Delta/2pi = 22.1100 THz
     magnitudes-only misreading 1/(1/33 - 1/67) = 65.029 THz, a factor 2.941 in Delta and hence in Omega
  E_pi = pi^2 I_sat w^2 Delta / gamma^2 with I_sat = 1500 W/m^2, w = 10 um, gamma and Delta ANGULAR:
     Chain II (Omega = g^2/Delta,   as printed ~12 nJ): 13.561 nJ
     Chain I  (Omega = g^2/2Delta,  the plan's Section 13 row): 27.122 nJ
     ordinary-frequency gamma and Delta instead: 85.2 nJ  (the angular convention is load-bearing)
  I_sat conventions: paper-specific D1 value 150 mW/cm^2 against the two-level pi h c gamma/(3 lambda^3) at 369.5 nm = 50.77 mW/cm^2, a ratio 2.9545
  Hayes' E_0 is FLUENCE-normalized: int|f|^2 dt = E_0^2 tau exactly while the peak is f(0)/E_0 = sqrt(pi/2) = 1.25331414
     feeding a measured PEAK field or intensity in as E_0 overstates Omega_0 and Ibar by pi/2 = 1.5708
  fine structure omega_F/2pi = 100.109 THz; Delta/2pi at 355 nm = 33.197 THz
  second order at 200 mW / 3 um waist (Ibar = 2 Pbar/(pi w_0^2) = 1.415e+10 W/m^2, g_0/2pi = 73.2 GHz):
     E^(2)_00/2pi = +104.0 kHz  (a residual of 1/Delta = 4.7943e-15 against 2/(omega_F - Delta) = 4.7571e-15)
     delta_omega^(2)/2pi = -7.63 kHz   (Lee prints -7.3 kHz, an ORDINARY frequency)
     with Pbar/(pi w_0^2) instead of the peak on-axis intensity: -3.82 kHz -- a factor-2 diagnostic
  Delta_D1 = Delta_FS/3 is the exact zero of E^(2)_00 alone: lambda = 354.93 nm
     normalized differential shift (delta_0 - delta_1)/Omega_0,1: 1.8944e-04 at Delta_FS/3, 1.7860e-04 at (sqrt2 - 1) Delta_FS (lambda = 351.6 nm), i.e. 5.7% lower -- '355 nm is the minimum' is approximate

== 6. Fourth-order (intensity-squared) ac Stark shift and the comb factor C_{n,a} 
  int_0^inf sech^2(v) tanh(v)/v dv = 0.852556797635
  7 zeta(3)/pi^2                   = 0.852556797635   (printed 0.853)
  4 x that                         = 3.410227191   (printed 3.412, the two-comb smooth term)
  single comb at Omega_0/2pi = 1 MHz, tau = 10 ps, nu_rep = 80 MHz, n = 158:
     Eq. 27 exact symmetrized sum: delta_4/2pi = 7511.2 Hz
     Eq. 28 closed form:           delta_4/2pi = 8465.6 Hz   (printed +8.5 kHz)
     effective coefficient of the exact sum = 0.7564 against 0.85256  (omega_q tau/2 = 0.397 is not small)
     with the PRINTED coefficient 0.853 instead of 7 zeta(3)/pi^2 the closed form gives 8470.0 Hz, which is the brief's 8.470 kHz
  two-comb Stark-nulling offset sigma = omega_A mod omega_rep, over omega_rep:
     tau =    5 ps: Eq. 31 root sigma = 0.353353   exact Eq. 30 root sigma = 0.315397   (paper quotes ~0.35 and ~0.40)
     tau =   10 ps: Eq. 31 root sigma = 0.399342   exact Eq. 30 root sigma = 0.366248   (paper quotes ~0.35 and ~0.40)
     tau -> 0 limits: Eq. 31 gives 1/sqrt(12) = 0.288675, the exact sum gives 1/4  -- root-find on the exact sum, the closed form can differ even in sign near a null
  nearest beat-note order for the clock transition at nu_rep = 120 MHz: omega_HF/omega_rep = 105.3568 -> j = 105, residual delta_00,10/2pi = +42.8210 MHz
  k = 0 term alone = sech^2(j pi nu_rep tau) = 0.746343  (C is NOT normalized to 1)
  CONVERGENCE REGRESSION for C_00,10 -- assert the whole sweep, not successive agreement:
     |k| <=      0:  C_00,10 = 0.746343
     |k| <=      5:  C_00,10 = 0.453162
     |k| <=     10:  C_00,10 = 0.450920
     |k| <=    100:  C_00,10 = 0.669087
     |k| <=    500:  C_00,10 = 0.940671
     |k| <=   1000:  C_00,10 = 0.943780
     |k| <=   5000:  C_00,10 = 0.943789
     |k| <=  20000:  C_00,10 = 0.943789
     the |k| ~ 5-10 plateau is a factor 2.093 LOW against the converged value
  (g_F mu_B/h x 5 G with g_F = g_J/2 = 1.001128 gives 7.0060 MHz; the rounded 7.000 MHz is used below, which is what the brief's C values assume)
  C_00,11 : j =  105, delta/2pi =  +49.821 MHz, C = 0.894381
  C_00,1-1: j =  105, delta/2pi =  +35.821 MHz, C = 0.964856
  C_10,11 : j =    0, delta/2pi =   +7.000 MHz, C = 0.988841
  C_10,1-1: j =    0, delta/2pi =   -7.000 MHz, C = 0.988841
  -> j = 0 is the OPERATIVE case for the Zeeman terms and C_10,11 = C_10,1-1 exactly; a j != 0 guard deletes them and destroys the beta-hat cancellation.  Guard delta != 0.
  sigma_pm : beta-hat ratio of delta_omega^(4) = 1.9641  (Lee quotes 23/12 = 1.9167); regress on this ratio, not on 23/12 MHz absolute
  tau sensitivity of C_00,10 (the source's own tau-vs-bandwidth inconsistency):
     tau =    4 ps: C_00,10 = 0.7174
     tau =    7 ps: C_00,10 = 0.8204
     tau =   14 ps: C_00,10 = 0.9438
     tau =   20 ps: C_00,10 = 0.9332
  intensity-squared transfer: delta(delta_4)/delta_4 = 2 x delta(Omega)/Omega  (delta_4 ~ Omega_0^2 ~ Ibar^2)

== 7. Beat-note arithmetic: Hayes q, Islam lock, Inlek MS orders and PLL frequencies 
  Hayes q = nu_0/nu_R at nu_R =  80.780 MHz (free-running  ): 156.5090
  Hayes q = nu_0/nu_R at nu_R =  40.390 MHz (picked 1-in-2 ): 313.0181
  Hayes q = nu_0/nu_R at nu_R =  26.927 MHz (picked 1-in-3 ): 469.5213
     -> 156.5 (half-integer, no evolution), 313.0 (integer, Rabi flopping), 469.5 (half-integer, none)
  Islam: 157 x 80.6 MHz = 12.65420 GHz  (paper ~12.655 GHz); nu_ab/nu_rep = 156.8588 -> n = 157
     nu_M1 = n nu_rep - nu_LO = 216.200 MHz (paper ~217 MHz)/Users/churchill/.cache/uv/archive-v0/v6zNgoi5fEtIAa9p/lib/python3.13/site-packages/qutip/__init__.py:24: UserWarning: matplotlib not found: Graphics will not work.
  warnings.warn("matplotlib not found: Graphics will not work.")

     nu_M2 = nu_ab - nu_LO    = 204.819 MHz (paper ~205 MHz, the carrier)
     |Delta nu_M| = 11.381 MHz; nu_sb = nu_LO + nu_M2 = nu_ab exactly (drift-free)
     12.655 GHz / 157 = 80.6051 MHz recovers nu_rep
  Inlek Eq. 2 with n = 160 on the RED leg and m = 154 on the BLUE:
     nu_B,r = 173.370 MHz (paper ~173.4), nu_B,b = 160.030 MHz (paper ~160.0)
     swapping n and m misses each condition by 483.42 MHz -- a hard regression test
  Inlek Eq. A.1 at nu_MO = 12.606 GHz:
     nu_PLL1 = 160 nu_r - nu_MO = 285.20 MHz
     nu_PLL2 = nu_MO - 154 nu_r = 198.22 MHz
     carrier PLL3 = 157 nu_r - nu_MO = 43.49 MHz
     single-PLL variant at 12.566 GHz: 83.49 MHz
     nu_AWG,r = 111.83 MHz, nu_AWG,b = 38.19 MHz; the printed 116.8 / 43.2 MHz are each high by exactly 2 nu_alpha = 5.00 MHz
     loop closure: PLL1 - AWG_r = 173.37 MHz = nu_B,r; PLL2 - AWG_b = 160.03 MHz = nu_B,b
  Inlek carrier (Eq. 1): nu_0/nu_r = 156.917 -> p = 157, nu_B,1 - nu_B,2 = -6.67 MHz
  Mizrahi time-domain delay T = n/(f_hf + f_a) at n = 5.5, f_a = 489 MHz: 418.83 ps (printed 419 ps)
     hyperfine phase across it: omega_hf T = 33.27 rad; (omega_hf + omega_A) T = 2 pi x 5.5 = 34.558 rad exactly
  effective two-photon wavelength at a 90 deg crossing: lambda/sqrt2 = 251.0 nm
     wave-front tolerance Delta phi_M = 2 pi l sin(theta)/lambda' at l = 30 um, theta = 0.0200 deg: 15.02 deg end-to-end
     wave-front tolerance Delta phi_M = 2 pi l sin(theta)/lambda' at l = 30 um, theta = 0.0500 deg: 37.55 deg end-to-end
     wave-front tolerance Delta phi_M = 2 pi l sin(theta)/lambda' at l = 30 um, theta = 0.0133 deg: 9.99 deg end-to-end
     -> the source's own triple does not close (15.0 deg against a stated < 10 deg); theta < 0.0133 deg is what is needed, and the achieved 0.05 deg is 2.5x looser
  Hayes gate self-consistency: t_g = 108 us at nu_R = 80.78 MHz -> N = 8724 pulses; delta/2pi = 1/t_g = 9.259 kHz
     inverting delta = 2 eta Omega: Omega/2pi = 46.30 kHz, theta_p = Omega T = 3.601 mrad, so theta_p << 1 and the first-order truncation of Hayes Eq. 5 is justified
     Hayes' eta Omega/delta = 1/2 is the J = (1/2) sum-sigma normalization; halved on ingest to the plan's eta Omega/eps = 1/(4 sqrt K) (Section 13)
  sech^2 tooth-pair weight varies by 0.53% per unit tooth index at nu_rep tau = 1.68e-03, which is what makes a flat few-tone truncation legitimate

== 8. Lamb-Dicke parameters and the Hayes bare-k discriminator ==================
  Hayes 1.64 MHz, bare k              : x_0 = 4.246 nm, eta = 0.0751
  Hayes 1.64 MHz, sqrt2 k (90 deg)    : x_0 = 4.246 nm, eta = 0.1063
  Hayes 1.64 MHz, 2k (counterprop)    : x_0 = 4.246 nm, eta = 0.1503
  Mizrahi 743 kHz, 2k                 : x_0 = 6.308 nm, eta = 0.2233
  Campbell 500 kHz, 2k                : x_0 = 7.690 nm, eta = 0.2722
  -> Hayes' quoted eta = 0.1 closes only with Delta_k = sqrt2 k, so its 'k' IS the two-photon Delta_k
  Lamb-Dicke guard at Campbell's nbar = 40: eta sqrt(nbar+1) = 1.743 > 1  -> a truncated expansion is illegal there
  Hayes sideband-resolution threshold (omega_t T eta)^-1 at T = 12.4 ns, eta = 0.1: omega_t T = 0.1278, threshold = 78.3  ('N >> 80')

== 9. Comb noise channels: harmonic gain, per-tooth lock residuals, amplitude noise 
  harmonic gain on the beat note: delta nu_sb = n delta nu_rep with n = 157: 1 Hz/min -> 157 Hz/min = 2.617 Hz/s
     over a 3 ms Ramsey window that is only 0.0079 Hz -- drift alone cannot explain the ~3 ms unlocked coherence; the implied fast jitter is 53.1 Hz rms on the beat note, 0.338 Hz rms on nu_rep [derived]
     a 1e-7 fractional drift at 80 MHz: 8.0 Hz x n = 158 -> 1.26 kHz at the qubit
  per-tooth residuals under the Islam feed-forward lock (n = 157):
     tooth m = 156: lower sideband   -1 x delta nu_rep, upper  +313 x, bare  +156 x
     tooth m = 157: lower sideband   +0 x delta nu_rep, upper  +314 x, bare  +157 x
     tooth m = 158: lower sideband   +1 x delta nu_rep, upper  +315 x, bare  +158 x
     tooth m = 167: lower sideband  +10 x delta nu_rep, upper  +324 x, bare  +167 x
     -> the lock nulls only the selected tooth's LOWER sideband; upper sidebands are worse than unlocked
  eps = (pi^2/2) alpha Omega_0^2 T at alpha =   -90.0 dB/Hz, Omega_0 = 600 kHz, T = 1 ms:  Hz reading 1.7765e+00   rad/s reading 7.0135e+01
  eps = (pi^2/2) alpha Omega_0^2 T at alpha =  -115.0 dB/Hz, Omega_0 = 600 kHz, T = 1 ms:  Hz reading 5.6179e-03   rad/s reading 2.2178e-01
  eps = (pi^2/2) alpha Omega_0^2 T at alpha =  -120.0 dB/Hz, Omega_0 = 600 kHz, T = 1 ms:  Hz reading 1.7765e-03   rad/s reading 7.0135e-02
     ratio = (2 pi)^2 = 39.478; structurally pi^2/2 = (2 pi)^2/8 = 4.9348022005
     exact 1% boundary: alpha = -112.50 dB/Hz, so the quoted -115 dB/Hz carries 2.50 dB of margin
  rep-rate sensitivity of the fourth-order shift (a deliberately off-resonant Stark drive):
     dnu/nu = 1e-06: d(delta_4)/delta_4 = +3.6018e-04  -> gain 360.2x
     dnu/nu = 1e-05: d(delta_4)/delta_4 = +3.6069e-03  -> gain 360.7x
     dnu/nu = 1e-04: d(delta_4)/delta_4 = +3.6605e-02  -> gain 366.0x
     the detuning term alone gives j nu_rep/delta_00,10 = 294.2x; the rest is C's own nu_rep dependence

== 10. Spin-dependent kick: Jacobi-Anger, U_SDK algebra, the blue-sideband sqrt(n+1) 
  Jacobi-Anger, exponent coefficient z = 1.17:  residual with J_n(z) = 8.44e-15, with J_n(z/2) = 3.28e-01
  -> the Bessel argument EQUALS the exponent coefficient; carry one symbol Theta_B defined as that
  higher-order suppression at Theta_B = pi/8: J_2/J_1 = 0.0988  (n_max = 3-4);  at Theta_B = pi: 1.7056  (truncation fails)
  U_SDK with the minus relative sign: |U^dag U - 1| = 1.30e-14
  U_SDK with the plus  relative sign: |U^dag U - 1| = 1.30e-14
     anti-Hermiticity |U^dag + U| = 0.00e+00; |U^2 + 1| = 1.30e-14
     |exp((pi/2) U) - U| = 1.02e-14  -> total train area pi, which is why sum_k Theta_B,k = pi
  blue-sideband generator M: |M - M^dag| = 0.00e+00; diag(M^2) first entries = [0.0, 1.0, 1.0, 2.0, 2.0, 3.0, 3.0, 4.0]
  -> M^2 = n_hat + 1 on one spin block and n_hat on the other, so the printed cos/sin closed form is exact only on the n = 0 manifold; the rate carries Theta eta sqrt(n+1)

done.
